diff --git a/docs/ARM_SPRITE_KERNELS.md b/docs/ARM_SPRITE_KERNELS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e360349
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ARM_SPRITE_KERNELS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# AArch64 sprite kernels
+
+The HLE PPU's sprite mask and shift operations use eight-byte AArch64 NEON
+vectors when `__aarch64__` and `__ARM_NEON` are present. Existing x86-64 SSE2
+and portable implementations remain available. `NESRECOMP_PPU_HLE_FORCE_PORTABLE`
+forces the scalar reference, including on ARM. No architecture header is
+included on an unrelated target.
+
+The kernel loads exactly eight lanes, tests counters before decrementing,
+uses unsigned saturating counter subtraction and shifts only ready sprite
+planes. A weighted horizontal reduction packs the eight high bits into the
+existing priority mask. The HD recorder's shift mask retains the same meaning.
+No guest clock, bus access, mapper behavior, save field or game routine changes.
+
+`cyc_ppu_kernel_test` compares native/scalar operations over every planar row,
+all simultaneous lane masks, all byte-valued counters at every lane and 250,000
+random configurations, including rendering-off and skipped-dot cases.
+`cyc_ppu_span_reference` now explicitly forces portable kernels, so its complete
+machine comparison also checks SIMD against scalar processing. Native interval
+and raster interval tests continue to pass.
+
+Two supplied games retain their 1,800-frame traces, native/interpreter parity,
+state continuation, untraced pixels, PCM and PNG. A separate MesenCE PAL capture
+matches 903 consecutive first-level frames after pre-input boot calibration.
+SDK GCC-generated kernel objects also pass the pure-kernel test under ARM64
+Linux with a test-only assertion bridge; that checks generated instructions,
+not libnx lifecycle or physical-console performance.
+
+Balanced Mac measurements show about 4.80% less process CPU for the tested PAL
+route. Mario's 1.09% result falls inside its A/A noise and is not a demonstrated
+desktop speedup. Switch Cortex-A57 performance still needs measurement. These
+kernels are a shared optimization, not a full-speed or visual-glitch fix claim.
diff --git a/docs/CORE_PROFILER.md b/docs/CORE_PROFILER.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a2ad8c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CORE_PROFILER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Optional device-clock host-time profiler
+
+Configure a cycle game with `NESRECOMP_CORE_PROFILER=ON` to compile diagnostic
+sampling around hardware clock calls. The default is OFF. Disabled builds have
+no counters, clock callbacks or sampling branches in `hw_machine.c`.
+
+This feature is independent of title hardware profiles and static game modules.
+The frontend supplies a monotonic clock: the Switch SDL host uses
+`SDL_GetPerformanceCounter`; the headless cycle host uses its existing monotonic
+wall clock. Other hosts can use `cyc_profiler_set_clock()` and
+`cyc_profiler_report()`, supplying matching timer units/frequency. The hardware
+implementation has no SDL/libnx dependency. Timers and counters are outside
+the guest state and save domain.
+
+Six clock-call paths are sampled: PPU dot, half-dot, CPU-tail and native interval;
+APU cycle and native interval. Counts include every call in enabled builds.
+Only sampled calls read the host clock. Xorshift-selected gaps of 1–2048 calls
+avoid period aliasing with guest scanlines or audio clocks. Startup measures
+the mean cost of 1,024 empty scopes, including coarse/fractional counter ticks.
+Timer correction happens after averaging, avoiding per-sample clamp bias.
+
+`estimated_ms` uses the median of nine interleaved sample-group means, then
+extrapolates to all calls and divides by completed frames. `mean_ms` also shows
+the raw mean, including scheduler pauses. The robust estimate limits isolated
+outliers, but can downweight rare genuine expensive work too: inspect both and
+repeat measurements. Path boundaries are exclusive at this integration
+layer, but include any device/mapper/interrupt work performed inside the called
+function. The reported residual is not pure CPU time: it also includes bus and
+frontend work plus profiling overhead. Sampling, timer resolution, compiler
+spills, caches and preemption introduce error; a negative residual is possible.
+Use enough samples/repeated windows and validate rankings against an unprofiled
+control. Do not report diagnostic FPS as production performance.
+
+The sampler does not skip device clocks or guest accesses. CTest
+`cyc_profiler_test` exercises calibration, sample counts/durations, reporting,
+reset and a missing clock using an original synthetic timer. The Switch host
+contract accepts `--profile-core` to check real sampled logs with SDL dummy
+drivers. Game validation should additionally compare full execution, untraced
+raw frames, PCM and state continuation with the profiler disabled.
